  "worked_solution": "We are given the complex number $z=-2.$\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=-2,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the point are $(-2,0)$, as shown in the Argand diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/556993791d4f77a087930583b910b06c92248b9a883d1c1358cfd6b081c572fb.png)",
